{"step_index":1200,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T23:34:56Z","thinking":"**Investigating Monotonic Clocks**\n\nI'm currently checking how monotonic timer functions are handled in Zig 0.16. I'm focusing on `@import(\"std\").time` and POSIX `clock_gettime`. Specifically, I'm now looking into standard POSIX implementations and `@import(\"std\").posix.clock_gettime`, as well as updating `ops/runtime/volatile_c`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"// ops/runtime/volatile_crdt_proof.zig\\n// Un-Elided Volatile Blackbox Readback Benchmark for Sovra CRDT Graph\\n// Forces volatile memory writes on every iteration to prevent LLVM Dead Code Elimination (DCE).\\n\\nconst std = @import(\\\"std\\\");\\nconst print = std.debug.print;\\nconst crdt = @import(\\\"sovra_crdt_kernel.zig\\\");\\n\\nconst c = @cImport({\\n    @cInclude(\\\"time.h\\\");\\n});\\n\\nfn getNanos() u64 {\\n    var ts: c.struct_timespec = undefined;\\n    _ = c.clock_gettime(c.CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts);\\n    return @as(u64, @intCast(ts.tv_sec)) * 1_000_000_000 + @as(u64, @intCast(ts.tv_nsec));\\n}\\n\\nfn volatileWrite(ptr: *volatile u64, val: u64) void {\\n    ptr.* = val;\\n}\\n\\npub fn main() !void {\\n    print(\\\"==========================================================\\\\n\\\", .{});\\n    print(\\\" UN-ELIDED VOLATILE BLACKBOX READBACK CRDT BENCHMARK (M4)\\\\n\\\", .{});\\n    print(\\\"==========================================================\\\\n\\\\n\\\", .{});\\n\\n    var graph = crdt.SovraCrdtGraph.init();\\n\\n    // 1. Warmup Iteration (10,000 insertions)\\n    var w: u64 = 0;\\n    while (w < 10000) : (w += 1) {\\n        _ = graph.insert_node(w + 1, .Episode, @as(u8, @intCast(w % 255)), 0);\\n    }\\n    graph.node_count = 0; // Reset arena\\n\\n    // 2. Volatile Sink setup\\n    var volatile_checksum: u64 = 0;\\n    const volatile_ptr: *volatile u64 = &volatile_checksum;\\n\\n    // 3. High-resolution Monotonic Nanosecond Timer\\n    const t0 = getNanos();\\n\\n    var i: u64 = 0;\\n    while (i < 100000) : (i += 1) {\\n        const ok = graph.insert_node(\\n            i + 1,\\n            if (i % 3 == 0) .Episode else .Semantic,\\n            @as(u8, @intCast(i % 255)),\\n            if (i > 0) i else 0,\\n        );\\n        if (ok) {\\n            // Force a volatile store to memory on every loop iteration\\n            volatileWrite(volatile_ptr, volatile_ptr.* +% graph.nodes[graph.node_count - 1].version_vector +% i);\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    const t1 = getNanos();\\n    const total_ns = t1 - t0;\\n    const total_us = total_ns / 1000;\\n    const ns_\n<truncated 678 bytes>","Description":"\"Writing un-elided volatile CRDT proof using POSIX clock_gettime\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/ops/runtime/volatile_crdt_proof.zig\"","toolAction":"\"Writing volatile CRDT proof using clock_gettime\"","toolSummary":"\"Writing volatile CRDT proof using clock_gettime\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
